Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.560
Speaker 1: I want to start today with a correction&nbsp;
if I get something wrong or if I'm not clear or if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.440
I'm incomplete about something, I always try to do&nbsp;
these at the top of the show. I have no intention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:17.120
of hiding the corrections on the back page, so&nbsp;
to speak, as is often the case with newspapers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:23.120
or other publications. So let me get right into&nbsp;
that. Yesterday, I did this segment about Fox&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:29.040
News propagandist Tucker Carlson siding with&nbsp;
Vladimir Putin and sort of writing off Ukraine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:35.760
saying Ukraine isn't even a democracy and sort&nbsp;
of softly justifying or defending or excusing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:42.400
Vladimir Putin's invasion of Ukraine. And I made&nbsp;
a lot of critiques of Ukraine in that segment that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:49.280
are true, including that there are concerns in&nbsp;
Ukraine about women's rights. There is corruption&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:56.000
in Ukraine. There's a lack of true rule of law in&nbsp;
Ukraine, a number of other concerning elements in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.880
Ukraine. But I didn't make clear that Tucker is&nbsp;
wrong about Ukraine not being a democracy. Ukraine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:10.880
is a democracy more or less. And certainly&nbsp;
way more than Russia is. If you look at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:19.120
Freedom Index Freedom House Dawg, you'll see that&nbsp;
Ukraine is a 60 out of 100 on the Freedom Index,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:27.360
which is sort of a measure of democracy. Russia is&nbsp;
a 20, so 60 puts Ukraine as partly free toe puts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:37.120
Russia as not free. So if I didn't make clear or I&nbsp;
misstated, Ukraine is a democracy, albeit a flawed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:42.800
one, and Ukraine is moving in the direction&nbsp;
of being more democratic, whereas recently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:48.800
Russia has moved in the direction of being less&nbsp;
democratic. The Ukrainian president Zelensky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:55.920
genuinely won an election, a real election he's in&nbsp;
over his head for sure. There were some problems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:02.480
with the election, but it was. He won. He he won.&nbsp;
He did not control the election in the way that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:09.040
Vladimir Putin controls elections in Russia. And&nbsp;
so this is a correction. I didn't make that clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:15.920
yesterday. Zelensky is not an authoritarian&nbsp;
autocrat. Vladimir Putin is, and that is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:22.480
crucial difference between Russia and Ukraine. It&nbsp;
doesn't resolve any other issue. It doesn't excuse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:28.800
the things that are not OK in Ukraine. But I&nbsp;
appreciate the opportunity to make that correction

